>> title: Brunswick Stew
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, chicken, tomato, corn, stovetop
>> counters: Smokehouse, One Pot
>> aka: brunswick, bbq stew, barbeque stew, pit stew, camp stew
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> pairs-with: skillet-cornbread
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven

>> step: sweat in a Dutch oven, 8 min
Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(diced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) in a #Dutch oven{} over medium heat for ~sweat{8%min}, until it goes soft without colouring.

>> step: simmer 20 min
Simmer @&(~1)onion{} with @chicken stock{4%cups}(950 mL), @crushed tomatoes{28%oz}(795 g), @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%Tbs}, and @hot sauce{2%tsp} for ~simmer{20%min}.

>> step: add the potato, simmer 25 min
Add @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; 1/2-in dice) to @&(~1)broth{} and ~simmer{25%min}, until they start to break at the edges and thicken it.

>> step: stir in the meat and the beans, simmer 30 min
Stir @chopped smoked pork{12%oz}(340 g), @smoked chicken{12%oz}(340 g; pulled), @baby lima beans{2%cups}(280 g; frozen), and @corn kernels{2%cups}(300 g) into @&(~1)stew{} and ~simmer{30%min}, stirring at the bottom so it does not catch.

>> step: season
Season @&(~1)stew{} with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, and @dark brown sugar{1%Tbs}.
